{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And I will remember My covenant with Jacob, etc.</b> The reason He mentioned the patriarchs in reverse order is that in every single generation Israel consume from the merit of the patriarchs; therefore He mentioned them in reverse order, in the manner of 'not only this, but even that.' By way of parable: a man who has three pouches of coins, in each one hundred gold pieces, and he begins to disburse from the first pouch at the beginning of the month of Nisan, and from the second in the month of Iyyar, and from the third in Sivan — it is obvious that the later pouch will always be found to have more than the earlier pouch, from which he has already been disbursing for many days. Therefore He said: not only the merit of Jacob, who is mentioned last — it is obvious that its merit has not yet been entirely consumed, for it is recent; but even My covenant with Isaac, which preceded Jacob, and concerning whom many days have passed for Israel who have been consuming his merit — for even his seed immediately and at once began to consume from his merit — you might suppose that it has already been consumed; therefore Scripture says: ״וְאַף אֶת בְּרִיתִי יִצְחָק״; and not only Isaac, but even the covenant of Abraham, which is very old and ancient — you might suppose that it has already been consumed; He makes known to us: ״וְאַף אֶת בְּרִיתִי אַבְרָהָם״ — that his merit is preserved for every single generation." "<b>And I will remember the Land.</b> For the Land has grounds to complain and to say: if Israel sinned, behold the Land — what is its transgression? For the plagues of the Land are brimstone and salt, burning the whole land, etc. (Deuteronomy 29:22), and it is written there (29:23): ״וְאָמְרוּ כָּל הַגּוֹיִם עַל מֶה עָשָׂה ה׳ כָּכָה לָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת״ — that is to say, the Land, what is its transgression and its sin. And so the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said (Nedarim 81a) that the question 'עַל מָה אָבְדָה הָאָרֶץ' — the prophets and the ministering angels were unable to explain, etc., as will be explained below in the portion of Nitzavim with the help of HaShem. Therefore it is said: ״וְהָאָרֶץ אֶזְכּוֹר״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:38:55.581860043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}